+## Definition of done for this standalone release
+
+- Callable finite reference components are wired through OneIGPU, not merely listed.
+- Existing exact primitives and legacy tests remain intact, with truthful CPU labels and actual record verification.
+- Search has an explicit budget; unknown/failing search never invents a solution.
+- Mining evaluates real SHA256d and independently rechecks found proof; no Lucas certificate is treated as Bitcoin work.
+- Checkpoints survive a close/reopen, and evidence changes are detected by replay.
+- Added tests exercise reference vectors plus generated adversarial/invariant fixtures; “all tests use real data” is not claimed.
+- Wider production/hardware requirements remain explicitly gated instead of being faked as complete.
